What changed: PeriodReopenController (apps/api/src/periods) adds
POST /periods/:periodId/reopen-requests {to_status, reason},
POST /periods/reopen-requests/:requestId/approve and
GET /periods/:periodId/reopen-requests. The mutations need period.reopen,
a 300 s step-up and the SoD engine (SOD_PERIOD_REOPEN_SELF_APPROVAL), and call
@ledgerforce/ledger requestReopen/approveReopen (migration 0018 repeats
every check and writes the audit rows). Replays are recognised by state.
The api-db test SS-UC10-06 (11 cases) and a routes.test.ts access assertion
come with it. nginx proxies /periods (SS-PLAT-86). ADR-0056 (Proposed), DL-0420,
DL-0421 (a close checklist after reopen needs schema: reported, not built).
This commit completes WIP 4e1d83d, which the lead saved at the usage limit.

Why: Design §3.5, §6.2 and §6.5 rule 6; UC-10 A3. The database layer existed
but there was no HTTP route.

Validation: RED saved first (.agent/evidence/T-0079/red-SS-UC10-06.txt:
11/11 failed with 404, because the routes did not exist). GREEN:
pnpm -s typecheck exit 0; pnpm -s lint exit 0; pnpm -s format:check clean;
VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 pnpm exec vitest run --project api-unit --project api-db apps/api
→ 34 files, 321 passed, 0 skipped. The first full run failed
nginx-routes.test.ts (periods not proxied); fixed in this commit.
verify.sh and cross-review have not run.

Next action: record evidence (evidence:tests --require SS-UC10-06), update the
register row and the card; the lead decides the checklist-round migration (DL-0421).

